{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774385040,"nonce":"F0PvU/kEXruyomz+DvRLOZR0Yus=","title":"Successful review exits misclassified as orphans due to status race","message":"When a review session completes successfully (outputs @@DONE@@, exits cleanly with subtype=success), there's a race between:\n1. The container exiting and being removed\n2. The session status transitioning from \"working\" to \"waiting:review\"\n\nThe orphan detector (check_orphaned_sessions) sees \"container gone + status working\" and counts it as an orphan restart. After 3 such cycles, the review session hits MAX_ORPHAN_RESUMES and gets suspended:review-failed — even though every run completed successfully.\n\nEvidence from review-c878c2506ab2 in jessica-ng:\n- All 3 exits were subtype=success (turns: 7, 11, 18)\n- All output @@DONE@@ correctly\n- orphan_resumes reached 3 → suspended:review-failed\n\nORPHAN_GRACE_PERIOD_S (120s) should prevent this but doesn't help because the review container runs, finishes, and is removed quickly — it's not \"recently launched\" by the time the orphan check runs.\n\nPossible fixes:\n- Post-run status update must happen before the container is removed (or atomically with it)\n- Orphan detector should check if @@DONE@@ was emitted in raw-output.log before classifying as orphan\n- Add a \"completed_at\" timestamp to state.json during post-run, and skip orphan check if recently completed\n- Review sessions that exit successfully should transition to waiting:review inside the container (in entrypoint/SessionRunner) before the process exits, not in the host watcher","files":null}]}